fact WorkItem(id: "WI-711", description: some(value: "Unify list's ready/blocked classification onto the KB rule; delete the is_satisfied/any_unmet operation mirror. PROBLEM: two copies of dependency-satisfaction/blocking logic exist and have already drifted. list (cmd_list_plain, main.anthill:1449) classifies rows via hand-rolled OPERATIONS is_satisfied(status)+any_unmet(deps,row_map)+partition_ready/blocked (main.anthill:911-937); the comment at main.anthill:917 admits it 'Mirrors the KB claimable rule'. next (cmd_next, main.anthill:2748) instead uses the KB RULE via execute(kb(),pattern_query(claimable(?id,?desc))) (main.anthill:2756), which leans on all_deps_satisfied/dep_satisfied in rules.anthill. DRIFT: the KB blocked rule gates on status:Open only (rules.anthill:54) whereas the op partition_blocked runs in EVERY status group (print_group_body applies it per group), so a PreOpened/Claimed item with unmet deps gets a '-- blocked --' line the rule would never emit -- two definitions that disagree. NOT rust-vs-anthill: both paths run entirely in the anthill bundle over KB facts (the mirror is anthill operations vs anthill rule); list sources rows via WorkItemStore.all -> facts_of(kb(),WorkItem) (eager whole-relation List[Term], store.anthill:228), next via execute(...) -> lazy Stream[Solution]; Rust supplies only leaf verbs (facts_of, execute, pattern_query, term_*, Map, Cell, println). So this is an anthill-only change: swap facts_of+hand-classify for execute(a blocked/has_unmet_deps goal), no host change. FIX: (1) rules.anthill add a STATUS-AGNOSTIC rule has_unmet_deps(?id):-WorkItem(id:?id,depends_on:?deps),(some ?d in ?deps: not(dep_satisfied(?d))), and redefine blocked as Open+has_unmet_deps; the bounded-quant (some/forall ?d in ?deps: ...) ALREADY resolves as a rule-body goal (some_in/forall_in, resolve.rs:1437), so all_deps_satisfied can also drop its hand-written all_deps_satisfied_rest recursion (rules.anthill:32-36) for a one-line forall-in -- no new capability needed. (2) cmd_list_plain runs has_unmet_deps(?id) ONCE via execute(kb(),pattern_query(...)) -- the single-query-collects-a-set pattern cmd_next already uses (main.anthill:2756-2759) -- collects the blocked id-set, and partition_ready/blocked classify rows by set membership (one SLD query for the whole set, not per-row). (3) delete is_satisfied+any_unmet and inline callers; KEEP the genuinely-functional row pipeline (unblocks aggregate via build_dep_map/count_transitive, has_feedback join via feedback_set, chrono_topo ordering, status grouping) -- those are not relational and stay (see backlog follow-up for turning them into queries too). DECISION: encode status-agnostic has_unmet_deps so every group's blocked partition is rule-derived (matches today's list behavior, removes the rule's Open-only limitation). depends-on-PreOpened=>blocked is already true in both list and next (empirically verified: an Open item depending on a PreOpened item shows under '-- blocked --', is refused by next, and is excluded from --unblocked); this WI must keep that invariant. ACCEPTANCE: one definition of dependency-satisfaction (the rule); list and next agree by construction; regression test pinning depends-on-PreOpened=>blocked in BOTH list and next; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh; /code-review run."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-13T13:19:15Z"))
